;; SW-169: `apply` resolving a builtin operator (as opposed to a user
;; closure) is a separate value-position route from the one LE-16 closed for
;; map/let/a user higher-order call, and had its own gap:
;; `(apply vector-copy (list v))` and `(apply car (list p))` silently
;; answered `()` -- exit 0, no exception -- instead of raising or computing
;; the right value. Fixed by giving CallApplyCodegen's builtin-operator
;; resolution the same fallback map already had (codegen_ast_callback_ ->
;; codegenVariable -> codegenInlineBuiltinAsValue / lookupInlineBuiltin),
;; rather than adding these three names to apply's own separate table.
(display (apply car (list (list 5 6)))) (newline)
(display (apply vector-copy (list (vector 1 2 3)))) (newline)
(display (apply vector-append (list (vector 1) (vector 2)))) (newline)
(define (my-double x) (* x 2))
(display (apply my-double (list 21))) (newline)
(display (apply + (list 3 4 5))) (newline)
